// The app target's base configuration, and the seam the RevenueCat key arrives through.
//
// This file is committed and always present, because `project.yml` names it in `configFiles`
// and XcodeGen refuses to generate a project whose config file is missing:
//
//     Target "Salus" has invalid config file path ".../App/Secrets.xcconfig" for config "Debug"
//
// The key itself is not committed. It comes from `Secrets.local.xcconfig`, which is git-ignored
// (`.gitignore`: `*.local.xcconfig`) and optional — `#include?` is the spelling that tolerates
// its absence, and the blank default below is what a build without one gets.
//
// To supply a key:
//
//     printf 'SALUS_REVENUECAT_API_KEY = <your key>\n' > App/Secrets.local.xcconfig
//
// A blank value is a legitimate build: `SalusApp.init` never calls `Purchases.configure`, every
// call in `RevenueCatPurchasesGateway` short-circuits to the safe free/no-offering state, the
// paywall surfaces "offering unavailable", and nothing crashes. `scripts/m9-manual-qa.md` §6 is
// where that build is walked by hand.

// The default, first: an xcconfig takes the *last* assignment it sees, so the include below has
// to come after this line to be able to win.
SALUS_REVENUECAT_API_KEY =

#include? "Secrets.local.xcconfig"
